      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Leptoancistrus canensis (Meek &amp; Hildebrand, 1913)</li><li>Synonym: Ancistrus canensis</li><li>Type locality: Río Cana, Cana, Darien, Panama.</li><li>Identification: the genus Leptoancistrus is characterized by having one or more very long cheek odontodes, and lacking adipose and anal fins.</li><li>IUCN Red List: Least Concern (last assessed 2019).</li></ul>"
